  "_title": "The clock — a machine needs a heartbeat",
  "_description": "A 555 wired as an astable, running at about 1 Hz, with an LED so you can see it. Everything after this rung moves only when this pin changes. Slow it down or speed it up by changing the capacitor: f = 1.44 / ((R1 + 2·R2)·C). Watching a computer at one step per second is the whole reason to build one out of chips.",
